  "topic": "inlay_hints",
  "subtopic": "type_hints",
  "title": "Types in templates",
  "summary": "A variable in a template shows its type as the template would write it",
  "prose": "A type that waits for an expression only instantiation can work out, such as `input + 1`, shows nothing, and neither does one the initializer already names. A template instantiated exactly once shows that instantiation's types instead.",
